<!--Post: 11170--><!--Time: 1110488905-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11170"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 1:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ember, the date was May 2nd or 3rd of 1993. I remember this because my 1st niece was born early the morning of May 4th and we went to have breakfast at Russel&#39;s that morning and people were talking about it, plus I remember seeing the article and a picture of the van in the paper that morning.  I do not have any links other than maybe looking in the archives of the Salina Journal....<a href="http://www.saljournal.com" target=_top>www.saljournal.com</a>.  I know she was a single mother with a daughter maybe a year or two younger than me...a friend of mine knew the daughter, but I never met her.  I do not know if she had any other kids.  I&#39;m sure she&#39;s probably listed in cold case files here in Kan.  How do I go about bringing this up to LE? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11170-->
<!--Post: 11173--><!--Time: 1110489270-->
