<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11223"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:williammichael@direcway.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 6:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Icyou, what street exits from I-135 are actually involved, and which cross streets &#40;east/west&#41; are in the immediate vicinity of the storage facility? <BR>I am looking at at map and from your description, it may be on Salemsborg Rd.  If so, exactly one mile south is the exit for FALUN road, which leads directly west to Falun, 7 miles away.  If my map reading is correct, the exit coming from the south which leads directly to the storage units is exactly the exit to take coming from Wichita to Falun.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11223-->
<!--Post: 11232--><!--Time: 1110516512-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11232"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 8:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good work Mike...I believe Centennial road turns into Salemsborg road when you take it South.  I don&#39;t know, I&#39;ll have to check it during the day.  That is interesting though.  It&#39;s completely feasible that he has evidence stored here in Salina.  When you come off the I-135 exit, you take a left onto Schilling Road in which you would be going west.  Then you take a right onto Centennial Road about 3/4 mile up Schilling Road.  My mileage calculating is merely estimates...but Centennial Road is very accessible after coming off of I-135.  I will check tomorrow to see exactly what the name of Centennial Road is going south...i do believe the name changes.  The Falun connection is interesting. Although  if Centennial Road does become Salemsborg Road...it leads to Falun Road which runs east/west and Falun is west.  Also, Skov, I did realize the glasses connection.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11232-->
<!--Post: 11235--><!--Time: 1110519912-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11235"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 9:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have been doing some of my own crazy map work on this, Mike I want to put the addresses of some of the Possilbe victims in the strange dates thread and I need you and Icyou to tell me if I am crazy or are all these addresses right off of 135. and if so where does 135 go<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11235-->
<!--Post: 11282--><!--Time: 1110555746-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11282"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 7:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->okay first....mike....I drove  Centennial Road this morning...it does not turn into Salemsborg Road, Salemsborg road actually intersects Centennial Road about 5 miles South of Schilling Road.  Did you say Salemsborg Road itself leads into Falun?  I did not have time to drive that far out. <BR> <BR>Ember,  yes this particular address is basically right off of 135.  It is very very close.  But the more I think about this...Ican&#39;t understand why her van would have been left in Russel&#39;s Restaurant parking lot because it is quite a ways north from there.  Also the more I think about it...the day she was last seen and the discovery of her van, there was too much time between the two...it doesn&#39;t sound like BTK.  I dunno.  I&#39;m thinking and analyzing too much about it.  Waht do you think about the evidence I&#39;ve given you? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11282-->
<!--Post: 11294--><!--Time: 1110561299-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11294"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 9:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am thinking at this point, if we don&#39;t ask the questions then we never find the answers lol keep thinking, the pieces are starting to come together.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11294-->
